Subject: [PATCH] TTA: give sub-384px images a second view instead of skipping TTA

Selective TTA currently requires `min(w,h) >= min_side` (384), because the
native view is a resampling-free centre crop and that crop does not exist for a
smaller image. The effect is that the second view is switched off for exactly
the images the model is least sure about -- thumbnails and avatars.

A smaller image has no resampling-*free* crop, but it does have a
*less*-resampled one: resize the shorter side to C (384) rather than to
resize_shorter_side (440), and centre-crop C. That is a genuinely different
view from the standard one -- less upscaling, full frame, no padding the model
has never seen -- and it needs no new preprocessing code, just `preprocess`
called with a different `resize_shorter_side`.

For `min(w,h) >= min_side` the behaviour is unchanged, bit for bit.

--- a/extension/src/offscreen.js
+++ b/extension/src/offscreen.js
@@
     // Selective TTA: when the standard view lands in the uncertainty band and
     // the image is large enough for a native crop, average raw logits with a
     // second, resampling-free view (measured: +0.9/+0.5/+0.3 balanced acc).
     let tta = false;
     const task = async () => {
       const zStd = await runLogit(input);
       const cfg = modelMeta.tta || {};
       const C = modelMeta.input_size;
       let z = zStd;
       if (cfg.enabled) {
         const s = calibrate(zStd, modelMeta);
-        if (s >= cfg.band_lo && s <= cfg.band_hi &&
-            Math.min(img.width, img.height) >= (cfg.min_side || C)) {
-          const zNative = await runLogit(preprocessNative(img, modelMeta));
+        if (s >= cfg.band_lo && s <= cfg.band_hi) {
+          // A sub-min_side image has no resampling-free crop, but it does have
+          // a less-resampled one: shorter side to C instead of S. Unchanged
+          // for images at or above min_side.
+          const big = Math.min(img.width, img.height) >= (cfg.min_side || C);
+          const secondView = big
+            ? preprocessNative(img, modelMeta)
+            : preprocess(img, { ...modelMeta, resize_shorter_side: C });
+          const zNative = await runLogit(secondView);
           z = (zStd + zNative) / 2;
           tta = true;
         }
       }
       return calibrate(z, modelMeta);
     };
